# DOPD (the difference of two OPD runs), SZCO, ZABERR (the selected Zernike content) and ZRM (the fitted modes
# removed) on the manual's Cassegrain after a 1e-4 rad tilt of the secondary (cmdref: Misc / Outputs).  NONE first.
# OPD before (1.29e-12) and after (3.566e-11); DOPD rms 2.454e-11; ZABERR of modes 4-6 (Noll) reads 4.347e-11
# of defocus/astigmatism content; ZRM of modes 1-3 leaves 3.565e-11.  Note (PLAN 1.2 (k)): a DOPD issued AFTER
# ZABERR/ZRM reports "RMS dOPD = -1.0" -- keep DOPD right after the second OPD.
# PIN POLICY (CC 2026-10-23, TO's question): the 3.5664D-11 after the tilt is a RESPONSE (28x the 1.29D-12
#   baseline, which is bounded), so it is pinned to five figures under rule 2 as a deliberate exception to the
#   1e-9 magnitude threshold of rule 1; arm64 shares the five figures (CCMac gate 10).  If arm64 ever moves it,
#   that is a cross-architecture trace difference at 1e-5 relative, worth a finding -- do not widen blindly.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
opd 5
perturb 3
global
1e-4,0,0
0,0,0
opd 5
dopd
szco
cir
zaberr
3
4,5,6
no
zrm
3
1,2,3
no
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+\d\.\d+D-1[2-9][\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+3\.5664\d*D-11
# EXPECT: RMS dOPD =\s+2\.454\d*E-011
# EXPECT: Set to using NormNoll
# EXPECT: RMS WFE \(after ZAB\) =\s+4\.347\d*E-011
# EXPECT: RMS WFE \(after ZRM\) =\s+3\.565\d*E-011
# (the 1e-11 lines: four figures -- arm64 reads 3.566438007 against 3.566435264 on the secondary RMS, CCMac's gate 3)
# EXPECT-NOT: Must run OPD command first
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
